# MSSP Control Plane — Always-Applied Project Rules

Full detail: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTEXT.md`, `docs/KB036_MSSP_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_ROADMAP.md`.

**Source of truth:** Git tags/commits and validation-script PASS lines beat stale docs.

## Project Summary

- **Enterprise open-source MSSP / SOC / MDR / XDR platform** — not a Wazuh dashboard, not Streamlit-as-product.
- **MSSP Control Plane** (FastAPI + PostgreSQL + Redis + admin/customer UIs on VM 100) is the **production product**; engines are backend adapters only. Same design migrates to cloud later.
- **On-prem local servers now = production path** (complete end-to-end MSSP). Not a disposable lab. Every backend tool, wiring, config, and security control must be **enterprise-ready** (or an explicit dated gap + upgrade path).
- **Approved enterprise stack (KB-036 roadmap):** Wazuh, Suricata, Zeek, TheHive, Shuffle, MISP, Greenbone/OpenVAS, Velociraptor; Ansible/Compose; Prometheus/Grafana.
- **Vuln scanners:** **Nuclei + Vuls** on VM 109 with Greenbone CE (KB-078); never on control plane; Greenbone Enterprise deferred (KB-077).
- Deployment models: **cloud-hosted**, **on-prem appliance**, **hybrid**.
- Multi-tenant; admin/SOC cross-tenant where role allows; customers tenant-isolated only.
- **No lab/demo wording** in dashboards or runtime defaults (fail-closed tenant mapping; `THEHIVE_DEFAULT_ORG` default `MSSP`).

## Current State

